# Campaign & Creation File management (AI instructions)

Complements `preserve-and-expand`, `dm-management-system`, and `cmdb-configuration-items`. Expand the CMDB; do not replace it.

## Core principles

- Every stored row is a **Creation File (CF)** with one `ciClass` and one category (`src/lib/ciRegistry.ts`).
- **Campaign** (`campaign.record`) is the structural root: id links to party, seeds, results, characters, items.
- Relationships are **id references owned by the container**; reverse lookup via `src/lib/ciRelationships.ts`.
- **Manual-first** (`dm-control-tower`): every AI feature needs a non-AI path.
- **SRD compliance**: bundled rules are read-only; user-owned content stays in imports/creations.

## Library (“The Library”) — preserve all shelves

Existing shelves stay: All, CFs, Prepared scrolls, Heroes, Items, **Rule tomes**, Fellowships, Chronicles. Add views (graph, timeline, session log) as **new** panels — never remove a shelf.

## Domain responsibilities (additive)

| Domain | Store today | AI may add |
|--------|-------------|------------|
| Campaigns | name, description, id links | arcs, quests, unresolved threads, continuity hints |
| Characters | `character.sheet`, party snapshots | level-up hints, rule flags, backstory hooks |
| World assets | often in `seed.*` / `result.*` markdown | future `location.*`, `npc.*`, `faction.*` CF classes |
| Adventures | `seed.adventure`, `result.adventure` | auto-link referenced assets, quest state |
| Encounters | VTT + markdown | future `encounter.*` CF; CR hints |
| Sessions | `session.tabletop`, `session.snapshot` | future `session.record` log CF |

## Metadata (extend, don’t break rows)

Optional fields for new/planned CFs (see `schemas/creation-files/`):

- `tags`, `status`, `relationships[]`, `owner`, `version` — add as optional; never require on legacy rows.

## Relationship graph (future)

Typed edges, e.g. `npc → lives_in → location`, `quest → involves → npc`. Implement **beside** campaign id lists; do not remove `seedIds` / `resultIds`.

## Session management (future)

Track events, NPC touchpoints, loot, locations, promises, clues. Summaries and “update affected CFs” — manual edit always available.

## DM tools to build toward

- Quick retrieval (“NPCs linked to faction X”)
- Auto-generation (optional AI) for NPCs, towns, hooks
- Consistency checks (lore, timeline, SRD, forgotten threads)
- Smart suggestions (non-spoiler by default)

## AI reasoning

- Interpret DM intent; preserve DM authority.
- No spoilers unless requested.
- Suggest — do not silently rewrite user CF markdown.

Schema reference: `schemas/creation-files/manifest.json`, `relationship-graph.json`.
